{
  "dqlnbVersion": 1,
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Your first hour",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Your first hour",
    "description": "Run the sample end to end: look at the orders table, reproduce the certified block's numbers, then write the SQL you want certified next."
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "about",
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "About",
      "source": "# Your first hour\n\nThis notebook runs against the workspace's default connection: the sample DuckDB file for the first hour (`sample/dql.config.duckdb.json`), your warehouse once `dql.config.json` points at it.\n\nEach person who runs these cells sees their own rows: in ZLens Enterprise, row rules and column policies set in the admin console apply to every query, including these."
    },
    {
      "id": "orders_sample",
      "type": "sql",
      "title": "Ten orders",
      "source": "SELECT order_id, customer_id, region, product, status, order_date, amount\nFROM orders\nORDER BY order_date DESC\nLIMIT 10"
    },
    {
      "id": "revenue_by_region",
      "type": "sql",
      "title": "Revenue by region (the certified block's SQL)",
      "source": "SELECT region, COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) AS order_count, SUM(amount) AS revenue\nFROM orders\nWHERE status <> 'cancelled'\nGROUP BY region\nORDER BY revenue DESC"
    },
    {
      "id": "revenue_by_month",
      "type": "sql",
      "title": "Revenue by month",
      "source": "SELECT date_trunc('month', order_date) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) AS order_count, SUM(amount) AS revenue\nFROM orders\nWHERE status <> 'cancelled'\nGROUP BY 1\nORDER BY 1"
    },
    {
      "id": "next",
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "Next",
      "source": "## Make the next answer certified\n\n1. Write the SQL here until it is right.\n2. Open a draft space (My draft spaces) or a branch on your laptop, and save it as a block under `domains/orders/blocks/` with the same fields as `revenue-by-region.dql`: owner, description, grain, outputs, sourceSystems, reviewCadence and a test.\n3. Mark it certified and submit for review. A steward approves the pull request; when it merges, Production follows main and Ask answers with the Certified label."
    }
  ]
}
